  "details": "Issue: When selecting a user to send a Boop to, the screen in which an emoji is chosen, can render overtop of UI elements on the Quick Menu.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Launch VRChat.\n\n2. Open the Quick Menu, and select a friend in the same instance, clicking on their capsule.\n\n3. Choose the \"Boop\" button for that user, if it is available.\n\n4. Be on the screen where you can select an emoji to boop towards a friend. Some UI elements are eclipsed, or cut off from view, which should not be the case.\n\nExpectations and observations:\n\n1. The \"Send Boop\" button at the bottom of the screen should be fully visible, and not cut off from the UI.\n\n2. UI elements at the top of the QM should be fully shown (or fully hidden), rather than being partially eclipsed.\n\n3. Opening the Quick Menu, and selecting the Social Tab in the Main Menu, then proceed to select any friend to boop does not trigger this bug; only through selecting a user's capsule and sending boops through the Quick Menu",
